<title>ITALY: Olivetti shares leap after Omnitel deal.</title>
<headline>Olivetti shares leap after Omnitel deal.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Italian information technology group Olivetti rose strongly in a generally lower Milan market after a deal on Friday to sell part of its stake in mobile phone consortium Omnitel, analysts and dealers said.</p>
<p>Olivetti sold an indirect 5.8 percent stake in Omnitel to German group Mannesmann for 432.5 billion lire, which will enable Olivetti to report a capital gain of 300 billion lire on it 1996 consolidated accounts.</p>
<p>&quot;It is undoubtably a positive operation from a financial point of view,&quot; said Andrea Beghetti, analyst at brokers Eptiasim.</p>
<p>At 1125 GMT, Olivetti shares were up 6.5 percent at 482.0 lire after hitting a high of 485 lire.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
